@startuml
title SD Host Controller - Command Inhibit (DAT) and Command Inhibit (CMD) Timing

skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam backgroundColor white

== Figure 2-11 : Timing of Command Inhibit (DAT) and Command Inhibit (CMD) with Data Transfer ==

robust "CMD line" as CMD1
robust "DAT line" as DAT1
binary "D00" as D00_1
binary "D01" as D01_1

@0
CMD1 is idle
DAT1 is idle
D00_1 is high
D01_1 is high

@5
CMD1 is Command

@15
CMD1 is Response

@25
CMD1 is idle

@30
DAT1 is "Write or Read Data"

@50
DAT1 is "Last Block Data"

@65
DAT1 is idle

@25
D00_1 is low

@65
D00_1 is high

@15
D01_1 is low

@25
D01_1 is high

== Figure 2-12 : Timing of Command Inhibit (DAT) for the Case of Response with Busy ==

robust "CMD line" as CMD2
robust "DAT[0]" as DAT2
binary "D00" as D00_2
binary "D01" as D01_2

@70
CMD2 is idle
DAT2 is idle
D00_2 is high
D01_2 is high

@75
CMD2 is Command

@85
CMD2 is Response

@95
CMD2 is idle

@95
DAT2 is Busy

@115
DAT2 is idle

@85
D00_2 is low

@115
D00_2 is high

@85
D01_2 is low

@95
D01_2 is high

== Figure 2-13 : Timing of Command Inhibit (CMD) for the Case of No Response Command ==

robust "CMD line" as CMD3
binary "D00" as D00_3

@120
CMD3 is idle
D00_3 is high

@125
CMD3 is Command

@145
CMD3 is idle

@125
D00_3 is low

@145
D00_3 is high

note right of D00_3
  The Host Controller clears D00
  if the command is issued successfully.
end note

@enduml